# ling.ignore — what `lingfu publish` leaves out of the root `ling-lang`
# tarball. Unlike `cargo publish` (which is git-aware and already skips
# everything .gitignore keeps untracked, e.g. ling-lang.org/), lingfu's
# tarball builder walks the raw filesystem with no git awareness at all — so
# large/non-essential content needs to be listed here explicitly, or it gets
# swept straight into the upload. Mirrors the crates.io `[package] exclude`
# policy in Cargo.toml (same "what's actually part of the distributable
# language/compiler" call already made there), plus a few purely-local /
# generated directories .gitignore already keeps out of git.

# Large or non-essential content (same policy as Cargo.toml's crates.io exclude)
assets/
examples/
docs/
instruments/
lexicons/
chinese-room-web/
recordings/
cache/

# The project website — gitignored, "published separately, not part of crate"
ling-lang.org/

# Build/VCS output (build_tarball also hardcodes skipping target/.git/dist/
# .ling-build/.ling-shared-target by name at any depth; listed here too for
# clarity and in case that hardcoded list ever narrows)
target/
dist/
.ling-build/
.ling-shared-target/
benchmarks/bin/
__pycache__/

# Editor / tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.github/

# Compiled/binary/media artifacts that shouldn't be in a source tarball
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.lib
*.wasm
*.pdb
*.rlib
*.rmeta
*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.flac
